AOT code caches: block tails in the data area, code mapped read+execute (FEX 14c9268, on top of 0003)

With AOTCodeCacheWIP, a block's JITCodeTail (entry RIP, spin lock, RIP
entries) no longer needs a GUEST_RIP_LITERAL. A RELOC_AOT_BLOCK_TAIL
relocation records where the tail is; when the cache is serialized the
block's JITCodeHeader is pointed at a copy of the tail in the data area,
which the loader fills in (RIP rebased, spin lock cleared).

When every relocation of a cache only fills the data area, LoadCache copies
the code once and maps it PROT_READ|PROT_EXEC; all pages count as loaded,
so nothing is relocated lazily. The SIGSEGV handler no longer treats a fault
in such code as a lazy page load, so a write into it is a real fault.

